  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposal is therefore NOT a lawful development.",
    "&lt;p&gt;Measuring off the applicant&#x27;s proposed elevation drawings officers have established that the proposed ground floor rear extension would incorporate an eaves height greater than 3m within 2m of the boundary of the curtilage. Furthermore the&amp;nbsp;submitted drawings fail to accurately reflect levels changes to the rear of the site,&amp;nbsp;so there is a possibility for the eaves height of the extension to be even greater than that depicted on the drawings. The proposed ground floor rear extension is therefore&amp;nbsp;not considered to be within&lt;span style=&quot;line-height:150%&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;the tolerances of Schedule 2, Part 1 Class A (i) of The Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
